# <type>(<scope>): <subject>
#
# <body>
#
# <footer>

# Types:
# feat:     A new feature
# fix:      A bug fix
# docs:     Documentation only changes
# style:    Changes that do not affect the meaning of the code
# refactor: A code change that neither fixes a bug nor adds a feature
# perf:     A code change that improves performance
# test:     Adding missing tests or correcting existing tests
# chore:    Changes to the build process or auxiliary tools
# ci:       Changes to CI configuration files and scripts
# build:    Changes that affect the build system or external dependencies
# revert:   Reverts a previous commit

# Scopes:
# action:   GitHub Action related changes
# types:    TypeScript type definitions
# docs:     Documentation changes
# config:   Configuration files
# workflow: GitHub workflows
# templates: Issue templates
# labels:   Label definitions
# seo:      SEO related changes

# Examples:
# feat(action): add story point detection
# fix(types): correct ActionInputs interface
# docs(readme): update installation instructions
# style(workflow): format YAML files
# refactor(action): improve label creation logic
# perf(action): optimize API calls with rate limiting
# test(action): add unit tests for auto-labeling
# chore(deps): update dependencies
# ci(changelog): add automated changelog generation
# build(npm): add TypeScript compilation
# revert(action): revert breaking change in v1.0.0 